From a7166284ee4a004869ee4fbce49b3ab041594618 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:30:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11-long CAL command mode (0029) - scripted decel
 levels through the full production envelope

The one calibration drive that pins the ESC brake constants (BITE / K in FCA11_ESC_BITE /
FCA11_ESC_K) needs the FCA11-long brake commanded at EXACT, scripted levels, independent of
whatever the planner asks. Today FCA11-long only actuates when the PLANNER asks for braking, so
there is no way to hold a clean 10 LSB step for a BITE fit.

This adds a file-gated, AUTONOMOUS calibration mode that sets the SOURCE of the FCA11 decel command
to an exact scripted level while every production gate stays on. Pure car-layer Python: no safety
model, no firmware, no panda change (the panda polices every frame exactly as for the planner's
asks).

Single-switch model: the whole cal path lives INSIDE the `if not self.enabled: return` guard of
Fca11LongBrake.update (self.enabled = CP_SP.fca11Brake and CP_SP.enableGasInterceptor). No separate
cal param, no bypass: if the owner's HyundaiFca11Brake toggle is OFF the state/plan file alone can
NEVER actuate, and turning the toggle off kills everyday FCA11 braking AND cal instantly.

New opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/cal_mode.py: a CalSequencer state machine ticked at 100 Hz from
the FCA11 update. It reads /data/fca11-cal/plan.json (the immutable rep matrix, written once) and
executes due reps opportunistically - engaged + band stable + feet off + no lead within
conditions.min_lead_m + near-straight (|v*yawRate| < turn_lat_max) - holding hold_s, then releasing
through the production fade. Progress (/data/fca11-cal/progress.json) is keyed by rep id and
persists across reboots; a new plan revision's NEW reps run, done reps never re-run. Self-
terminating (done=true). Plan absent/malformed/expired/TTL-stale OR a malformed progress file ->
INERT (byte-identical). A plan/file lapse MID-HOLD is an explicit veto (drops cal, production
release closes the episode the same frame). status() exposes a pre-flight summary (toggle,
plan validity, inert reason) for the operator, since the historic failure class here is silent
config state.

The scripted level acts as a FLOOR during a hold: dec_cmd = max(planner_ask, clamp(level, 2, 30)), so
cal can only ADD braking and can never silence a harder planner ask (e.g. a lead cutting in). The
level is clamped to the PANDA gate (HYUNDAI_FCA11_LONG_MAX_DEC = 30 LSB = 0.30 g), NOT the personality
tier cap - cal must reach 0.30 g regardless of the feel dial, and 30 is the personality-agnostic
firmware gate, so there is NO new authority. Entry is a CLEAN STEP through the existing
+HYUNDAI_FCA11_LONG_RATE_STEP (4 LSB) per SENT frame clamp (the fast panda-rate ramp, what the BITE
fit needs); release goes through the production fade/passive path unchanged.

Gas neutralization (REQUIRED): while a cal hold is active GasInterceptorCarController forces the
commanded pedal to 0. Without it the planner (holding cruise throttle at the start of a hold, then
seeing the car slow) commands gas, gas_pressed sets, and the panda's driver-cut latch cuts the very
episode being measured. It replicates the production condition (when the planner asks brake it
never gases) and can only REDUCE actuation; it is inert when cal is off. CarState still reports the
driver's pedal HONESTLY (the bus pedal during a hold is the driver's own input) so a driver
intervention stays visible in the logs. A same-frame gap between cal_active and the first dec_cmd
frame is avoided by aligning the sequencer decision to the 50 Hz SEND slot.

Every production veto still applies per frame: fca11_ok (engaged + heartbeat via the panda, gear D,
speed floor, camera not owning, driver-cut latches clear, pedal not faulted), the budget 2.5 s +
cooldown 3 s mirror, and the min-on/onset paths. A veto drops cal on the SAME frame.

Tests (test_fca11_long.py, single-file run): +20 new tests in TestCalModeGate / TestCalModeActuation
(plan absent/malformed/expired/TTL-zero -> inert; toggle OFF dominates a valid plan; level clamps to
30 regardless of personality; entry is a clean +4/frame step then a flat plateau; release is the
production passive frame; a driver cut cuts mid-hold; completion/reboot/revision idempotence; the
per-drive cap; the conditions gate; gas neutralization only during a hold; cal actuates with NO
planner ask). Whole file: 50 -> 70 passed. Falsifiable contrast: 13 of the 20 new tests FAIL on the
28-tree (the cal car-layer path is absent) and pass here.

Python-only, no opendbc/safety change (no firmware impact).
